.docs/plans/_archive/v0.13.8-shipped.md:3:**Thesis:** AppState is a 30-field god struct. Every subsystem — scheduler, capture loop, hygiene scanner, calendar poller, signal engine — reaches into the same monolith for its 2-3 dependencies. This makes it impossible to reason about what a subsystem needs, impossible to test subsystems in isolation, and creates implicit coupling between unrelated domains. Meanwhile, ~47 signal emission call sites across 15 files all manually import `crate::signals::bus::emit_signal_and_propagate` and pass `&state.signal_engine` — the last major module boundary without a service wrapper. This version does two things: (1) splits AppState into domain containers so the struct becomes a facade, and (2) formalizes the signal system behind a SignalService so callers stop reaching into bus internals. Both are mechanical refactors — no logic changes, no behavior changes. This is the last structural prerequisite before v0.14.0 feature work.
.docs/plans/_archive/v0.13.8-shipped.md:15:| I403 | SignalService formalization — wrap signals/ module behind a service API; eliminate direct `bus::emit_signal*` calls from all consumers | Refactor |
.docs/plans/_archive/v0.13.8-shipped.md:16:| I404 | AppState decomposition Phase 1 — core domain containers (Workflow, Calendar, Capture, Hygiene) | Refactor |
.docs/plans/_archive/v0.13.8-shipped.md:17:| I405 | AppState decomposition Phase 2 — integration and signal containers (IntegrationState, SignalState) | Refactor |
