.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:832:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:22:This ADR specifies the actor taxonomy, the propose/commit boundary, the contradiction-handling rules, the agent trust ledger, and the deduplication policy that collectively make humans and agents first-class, equal-structured claim sources. The substrate pieces needed in v1.4.0 are limited: an `actor` column and a `claim_state` column on `intelligence_claims`, plus the propose/commit state machine. The user-facing surfaces (Analysis Inbox, agent trust dashboard, contradiction resolution UI) ship in v1.5.0+ and are out of scope for v1.4.0.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:833:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:28:Every claim in `intelligence_claims` carries an `actor` string with one of the following canonical shapes. The `actor` column is non-nullable. Provenance's `Actor` type ([ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §1) uses the same shape.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:834:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:96:- **Transform abilities** produce `AbilityOutput<ClaimProposal>` — synthesized assertions with full provenance, but no side effect on `intelligence_claims`.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:838:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:168:Two committed claims at the same `(entity_id, claim_type, field_path)` with different `claim_text` are a contradiction. Contradictions are **never auto-resolved**. Both claims remain in `claim_state = 'committed'` with a contradiction marker:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:840:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:174:  claim_a_id      TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES intelligence_claims(id),
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:841:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:175:  claim_b_id      TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES intelligence_claims(id),
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:842:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:189:A claim is content-addressed by `dedup_key = hash(entity_id, claim_type, field_path, normalized_claim_text)`. Normalization includes trimming, Unicode normalization, and type-specific canonicalization (e.g., dates to ISO, names to case-folded).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:843:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:191:When a new claim is proposed whose `dedup_key` matches an already-committed or proposed claim in the active window (default 7 days, configurable per `claim_type`):
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:844:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:215:- `actor` column on `intelligence_claims` with canonical values from §1.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:846:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:295:**Consolidation timing — 2026-04-20 update:** Per plan-eng-review AskUserQuestion #1 and the brownfield-as-greenfield founder commitment (D1), consolidation ships in v1.4.0 as a destructive migration alongside the `intelligence_claims` table creation. Original R1.3 deferred consolidation to v1.4.1 out of migration caution; that deferral is retracted. Rationale: at AI velocity + minimal user base, keeping three parallel tombstone mechanisms alive through v1.4.0 creates interop cost that exceeds consolidation cost. The interop is what's expensive; one-table-to-rule-them-all is cleaner.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:847:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:302:- Reads switch to `intelligence_claims` for all tombstone queries.
