.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1360:.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:124:- v1.4.2 longitudinal topic work doesn't require a schema migration on `intelligence_claims`.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1364:.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:142:- [ADR-0113: Human and Agent Analysis as First-Class Claim Sources](0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md) — `intelligence_claims` row schema; this ADR adds one nullable column.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1503:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:8:**Consumed by:** [DOS-7](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-7) (`intelligence_claims.actor` column, tombstones), [DOS-241](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-241) (enrichment refactor design)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1505:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:15:2. [DOS-7](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-7) elevates `intelligence_claims` to a first-class table with per-claim identity and append-only assertion history.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1507:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:22:This ADR specifies the actor taxonomy, the propose/commit boundary, the contradiction-handling rules, the agent trust ledger, and the deduplication policy that collectively make humans and agents first-class, equal-structured claim sources. The substrate pieces needed in v1.4.0 are limited: an `actor` column and a `claim_state` column on `intelligence_claims`, plus the propose/commit state machine. The user-facing surfaces (Analysis Inbox, agent trust dashboard, contradiction resolution UI) ship in v1.5.0+ and are out of scope for v1.4.0.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1508:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:28:Every claim in `intelligence_claims` carries an `actor` string with one of the following canonical shapes. The `actor` column is non-nullable. Provenance's `Actor` type ([ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §1) uses the same shape.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1512:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:96:- **Transform abilities** produce `AbilityOutput<ClaimProposal>` — synthesized assertions with full provenance, but no side effect on `intelligence_claims`.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1517:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:174:  claim_a_id      TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES intelligence_claims(id),
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1518:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:175:  claim_b_id      TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES intelligence_claims(id),
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1522:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:209:[ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md)'s `DataSource` enum is **not** extended with new variants for actors. `DataSource` describes the *origin of information* (Glean downstream, Clay, Gong transcript, user input). `actor` describes *who asserted the claim*. A single agent claim has `actor = 'agent:prepare_meeting:1.3'` and sources `[Glean { downstream: Salesforce }, Glean { downstream: Gong }]`. The two axes are orthogonal and remain so.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1523:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:215:- `actor` column on `intelligence_claims` with canonical values from §1.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1527:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:295:**Consolidation timing — 2026-04-20 update:** Per plan-eng-review AskUserQuestion #1 and the brownfield-as-greenfield founder commitment (D1), consolidation ships in v1.4.0 as a destructive migration alongside the `intelligence_claims` table creation. Original R1.3 deferred consolidation to v1.4.1 out of migration caution; that deferral is retracted. Rationale: at AI velocity + minimal user base, keeping three parallel tombstone mechanisms alive through v1.4.0 creates interop cost that exceeds consolidation cost. The interop is what's expensive; one-table-to-rule-them-all is cleaner.
