.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-299.log:533:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:452:The earlier draft of this amendment said "Backfill of historical claims is a non-goal; `source_asof` stays NULL on pre-amendment rows." **That was wrong.** Adversarial review surfaced that the existing `ItemSource.sourced_at` field in stored `intelligence.json` blobs IS the evidence-time timestamp, and is consumed today by suppression (`is_suppressed`) and timeliness logic (`services/accounts.rs:1253-1274`). Treating migrated claims as unknown-timestamp would apply `STALENESS_PADDING` to data whose timestamp is actually knowable — that's a regression dressed as conservatism.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-299.log:534:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:457:backfill source_asof for each migrated claim:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-299.log:536:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:459:     → source_asof = parsed timestamp
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-299.log:538:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:461:     → source_asof = None AND emit ProvenanceWarning::SourceTimestampUnknown { fallback: ObservedAt }
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-299.log:540:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:472:The migration applies these bounds to every parsed `source_asof`:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-299.log:541:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:483:  - timestamp > now + 30 days (near-future; legitimate for renewal dates but suspicious for source_asof)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-299.log:542:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:485:    → freshness factor treats as observed_at instead
