.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:60:This is the pre-substrate version of what the substrate calls `SourceAttribution + source_asof`. It's already shipped, already populated by the LLM-prompt contract (`dimension_prompts.rs:608`), already consumed by `is_suppressed()` for tombstone-vs-evidence resurrection logic.
.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:62:**Implication for DOS-299:** the `source_asof` work isn't "build new substrate"; it's "promote ItemSource.sourced_at into a first-class column on the new claims table, and normalize the ~10 places that stamp `Utc::now()` to consult upstream timestamps instead." The semantics already exist in working code; the substrate is consolidating them.
.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:72:**Implication for DOS-7:** the propose/commit + tombstone-pre-gate substrate should **lean on `is_suppressed()`'s contract**, not reinvent it. Keep the existing function as the primitive; the substrate adds claim_state state machine + ledger around it.
.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:82:**Implication for DOS-7:** the migration story isn't "build claims table from scratch"; it's "extend the `account_stakeholder_roles` pattern across more claim types, then merge it into the unified `intelligence_claims` substrate." The pattern is proven. Use it as the precedent rather than treating claims as alien.
.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:166:The `entity_graph_version` / `entity_graph_sweep_state` triggers (migrations 113/117/121) are intelligent cache-busting infrastructure. Substrate writes to `intelligence_claims` need to participate in this cache invalidation — otherwise downstream caches miss claim updates.
.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:168:**Mitigation:** DOS-7 schema migration includes adding `intelligence_claims` to the entity_graph_version trigger set. Currently not in DOS-7 scope.
.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:172:The `account_stakeholder_roles → intelligence_claims` consolidation (DOS-7 §R1.3) writes to a table that's currently the source of truth for stakeholder reads. If the migration runs before reader migration, stakeholder pages break. If reader migration runs before write migration, stakeholder pages double-render.
.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:192:| 3 | `ItemSource` exists already | DOS-299 should explicitly call out that this is consolidation/promotion, not invention. Promote `ItemSource.sourced_at` into the first-class `source_asof` column; refactor the ~10 `Utc::now()` write sites; preserve `ItemSource` as the wire format for backward compatibility. | Update DOS-299 description |
.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:194:| 5 | `account_stakeholder_roles` is typed-row precedent | Add to ADR-0125 / DOS-300 references: cite this as the prior art. Use the same `data_source` column shape on `intelligence_claims` for consistency. | Update ADR-0125 references |
.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:197:| Knock-on B | Cache invalidation | DOS-7: add `intelligence_claims` to entity_graph_version triggers. | Spine spec adjustment |
.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:206:- **Runtime data quality audit.** This review is grep-based. Actual `SELECT COUNT(*) WHERE source_asof IS NULL` on the dev DB would change findings 3 and 6 from inferences to measurements. Optional Phase 2 if the user wants.
.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:208:- **Storage growth.** `intelligence_claims` + `claim_corroborations` + `claim_contradictions` + `agent_trust_ledger` + `claim_feedback` + `claim_repair_job` + invalidation_jobs is a lot of new tables. Bounded but worth measuring after the spine pilots run.
.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:225:1. **DOS-7 spec update:** scope tombstone consolidation across all 9 mechanisms (or explicitly split into v1.4.0 / v1.4.1 phases per-mechanism). Reference `is_suppressed()` as the pre-existing primitive. Add explicit phase ordering with soak windows. Add `intelligence_claims` to entity_graph_version triggers.
.docs/plans/storage-shape-review-2026-04-24.md:227:3. **DOS-299 spec update:** frame as "promote `ItemSource.sourced_at` into `source_asof`," not "build new field." Reference the ~10 existing `Utc::now()` write sites that need normalization.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/proof-bundle.md:102:- **DOS-347** (medium) — Serialize context-mode transition (DB persist + AppState swap). L2 cycle-4 surfaced this as a higher-level race at the command boundary; L6 ruled Option C (accept residual + follow-up). Not a substrate concern; lives naturally in W3/DOS-7's settings refactor scope. The substrate-level torn-bundle race (the actual W2-B concern) is structurally closed.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/proof-bundle.md:129:**Cycle 4 verdict (0fd17a36):** BLOCK with 1 HIGH — DB-persist + AppState-swap split across `set_context_mode` command without transition lock. **L6 Option C ruled** out-of-scope for v1.4.0 W2-B; filed as DOS-347 for W3/DOS-7's settings refactor scope.
