.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:451:22:This ADR specifies the actor taxonomy, the propose/commit boundary, the contradiction-handling rules, the agent trust ledger, and the deduplication policy that collectively make humans and agents first-class, equal-structured claim sources. The substrate pieces needed in v1.4.0 are limited: an `actor` column and a `claim_state` column on `intelligence_claims`, plus the propose/commit state machine. The user-facing surfaces (Analysis Inbox, agent trust dashboard, contradiction resolution UI) ship in v1.5.0+ and are out of scope for v1.4.0.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:452:28:Every claim in `intelligence_claims` carries an `actor` string with one of the following canonical shapes. The `actor` column is non-nullable. Provenance's `Actor` type ([ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §1) uses the same shape.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:455:42:- Parsing is strict: any claim with an unparseable actor is rejected at write time.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:456:46:Every claim carries a `claim_state` column with one of four values:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:459:55:Default reads use `claim_state = 'committed'` plus the `superseded_at IS NULL` filter from [DOS-7](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-7). History reads drop both filters.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:460:59:Commit policy is per-actor-class, declared in config, and applied at claim-write time:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:466:96:- **Transform abilities** produce `AbilityOutput<ClaimProposal>` — synthesized assertions with full provenance, but no side effect on `intelligence_claims`.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:469:101:Legacy path: where current enrichment writes claims directly (pre-v1.4.1), that write counts as a Maintenance ability call with a synthesized `ClaimProposal` and is subject to the same commit policy. The v1.4.1 enrichment refactor ([DOS-241](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-241)) is where this distinction becomes fully structural.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:472:110:- `claim_state = 'committed'` (tombstones commit immediately per §3)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:484:168:Two committed claims at the same `(entity_id, claim_type, field_path)` with different `claim_text` are a contradiction. Contradictions are **never auto-resolved**. Both claims remain in `claim_state = 'committed'` with a contradiction marker:
