.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1536:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:353:`corroboration_count` on the claim row becomes a cached denormalization (updated via trigger or on write) for query speed. Provenance of each corroborator is preserved. The trust compiler's corroboration factor reads from this table.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1537:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:363:- The "three tombstone mechanisms already exist" finding means the migration story is larger than v1.4.0 alone. Flag for [DOS-7](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-7) design review: decide whether v1.4.0 ships the `intelligence_claims` table + schema + service functions but keeps existing tombstone tables authoritative, with full migration to v1.4.1.
