.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:850:The earlier draft of this amendment said "Backfill of historical claims is a non-goal; `source_asof` stays NULL on pre-amendment rows." **That was wrong.** Adversarial review surfaced that the existing `ItemSource.sourced_at` field in stored `intelligence.json` blobs IS the evidence-time timestamp, and is consumed today by suppression (`is_suppressed`) and timeliness logic (`services/accounts.rs:1253-1274`). Treating migrated claims as unknown-timestamp would apply `STALENESS_PADDING` to data whose timestamp is actually knowable — that's a regression dressed as conservatism.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:855:backfill source_asof for each migrated claim:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:857:     → source_asof = parsed timestamp
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:859:     → source_asof = None AND emit ProvenanceWarning::SourceTimestampUnknown { fallback: ObservedAt }
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:870:The migration applies these bounds to every parsed `source_asof`:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:880:    → freshness factor treats as None (unknown) rather than honoring the implausible value
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:881:  - timestamp > now + 30 days (near-future; legitimate for renewal dates but suspicious for source_asof)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:883:    → freshness factor treats as observed_at instead
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:887:  - quarantined claims are queryable via `intelligence_claims WHERE provenance_warnings @> 'SourceTimestampImplausible'`
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:896:- Auto-classifier for inferring `source_asof` from claim_text content (v1.5.x+).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-211.log:897:- Backfill of `source_asof` from sources OTHER than existing `ItemSource.sourced_at` (e.g., re-fetching Glean documents to recover their timestamps for old claims). This is post-spine cleanup if needed.
