.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-210.log:545:298:**Rule 5 — Every ability output carries provenance via `AbilityOutput<T>`.**  
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-210.log:563:464:The original ADR defines `AbilityResult<T> = Result<AbilityOutput<T>, AbilityError>` but does not specify how abilities handle partial failure, composition failure, or soft degradation. The distinction matters because surfaces render different things based on outcome class.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-210.log:565:470:2. **Soft degradation** — ability returns `Ok(AbilityOutput<T>)` with `Provenance::warnings` populated. Output is usable; warnings tell the surface that parts were degraded. Examples: child Read timed out so context is thin; a stale source was included flagged as stale; LLM output anomaly was detected but the output itself still validated.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-210.log:566:472:3. **Hard success** — ability returns `Ok(AbilityOutput<T>)` with `warnings` empty (or only informational markers). Full output, no caveats.
.docs/decisions/0115-signal-granularity-audit.md:15:2. **Ability-output events.** [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) makes every capability a named, versioned ability producing an `AbilityOutput<T>`. Each output is cache-keyed and invalidation-tracked. "This output changed" is a new event class operating at ability-output granularity.
.docs/decisions/0115-signal-granularity-audit.md:35:| Ability output | `AbilityOutputChanged { ability_name, output_id }`, `AbilityOutputInvalidated` | 10³ / day |
.docs/decisions/0115-signal-granularity-audit.md:56:- **PropagateAsync { coalesce }** — emitted to the event log, an invalidation job is enqueued for each affected output. If `coalesce = true`, jobs for the same `(SignalType, EntityId)` collapse within a configurable window. Example: `EntityUpdated { coalesce: true }`, `ClaimTrustChanged { coalesce: true }`, `AbilityOutputChanged { coalesce: true }`.
.docs/decisions/0115-signal-granularity-audit.md:73:    (SignalType::AbilityOutputChanged,  PropagationPolicy::PropagateAsync { coalesce: true }),
.docs/decisions/0115-signal-granularity-audit.md:163:- Synthetic workload: 1,000 `ClaimTrustChanged` per minute + 100 `AbilityOutputChanged` per minute sustained for 10 minutes.
.docs/decisions/0115-signal-granularity-audit.md:269:**Also:** `SignalType` variants that carry data (e.g., `AbilityOutputChanged { ability_name, output_id }`) do not fit the `&[(SignalType, PropagationPolicy)]` slice shape. Use a function form instead: `fn policy_for(signal: &SignalType) -> PropagationPolicy` with an exhaustive match. The "const slice" in the original §3 is replaced by a function.
.docs/decisions/0115-signal-granularity-audit.md:299:`ClaimTrustChanged` uses `EntityAndField`. `AbilityOutputChanged` uses `OutputId`. `EntityUpdated` uses `EntityId` (current behavior). Per-type default in the registry, overridable by config.
.docs/decisions/0115-signal-granularity-audit.md:329:This ADR's Phase 0 is blocked on the `AbilityOutput` + `Provenance` types landing from [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) / [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) implementation. Document that dependency explicitly in [DOS-235](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-235)+.
