.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:183:The registry is the authoritative enumeration of abilities in the product. Because abilities have heterogeneous typed inputs and outputs, the registry cannot simply store function pointers in a `HashMap`. Instead, abilities are registered via a derive macro that generates a type-erased wrapper operating on `serde_json::Value`. The registry stores the wrappers and the schema metadata; consumers that want typed invocation go through a separate typed path.
